    pharm: "1. Fluids: 10 mL/kg 0.9% Normal Saline over 1 hour, then calculate deficit (10% dehydration = 100 mL/kg) and replace over 24-48 hours. Change to 5% Dextrose + 0.45% NaCl when glucose <250 mg/dL. 2. Insulin: IV Regular Insulin infusion at 0.1 units/kg/hour. Do not start insulin if K+ <3.3 mEq/L (correct K+ first). 3. Potassium: when K+ <5.5, add 20-30 mEq KCl per litre of IV fluid to maintain K+ 4-5. 4. Transition to subcutaneous: Insulin Glargine (once daily) + Insulin Aspart (with meals) when DKA resolved (pH >7.3, HCO3 >15, able to eat). Give Glargine 2 hours before stopping IV insulin.",
